  "created": "2026-05-11T16:51:20.003Z",
  "description": "A complete Domain-Driven Design (DDD) toolset for implementing domain models, including base types and source generators.\n\nhttps://github.com/TheArchitectDev/Architect.DomainModeling\n\nRelease notes:\n\n4.0.0:\n\nPlatforms:\n- BREAKING: .NET ⛔6-7 ✅8-10.\n\nThe base class is dead - long live the interface!\n- Feature: Generated [Wrapper]ValueObjects can now be structs. Unvalidated instances avoided via analyzer warning on `default`.\n- Feature: Generated [Wrapper]ValueObjects can now be records or use custom base.\n- BREAKING: [Wrapper]ValueObject gen replaced base class by interface. StringComparison property should drop \"override\" and become private.\n- BREAKING: Lack of ValueObject base class requires the string validation methods to be accessed via ValueObjectStringValidator class.\n- BREAKING: Entity<TId, TPrimitive> type params moved from base class to attribute.\n\nCompleted support for nested wrappers:\n- Feature: Nested Wrappers/Identities can now also convert, wrap/unwrap, and serialize/deserialize directly to/from their core (deepest) underlying type.\n- Feature: EF conversions for these now automatically map to/from the core type.\n- Feature: A different underlying type can be simulated, e.g. LongId : IIdentity<int>, ICoreValueWrapper<LongId, long>.\n- BREAKING: ISerializableDomainObject deprecated in favor of IValueWrapper, which represents any single-value wrapper.\n- BREAKING: IIdentityConfigurator/IWrapperValueObjectConfigurator now receive additional method type parameter TCore.\n\nCorrect string comparisons with EF via ConfigureIdentityConventions()/ConfigureWrapperValueObjectConventions():\n- Feature: These now set PROVIDER value comparer for each string wrapper property, matching type's case-sensitivity. Since EF Core 7, EF compares keys using provider type, not model type.\n- Feature: These now warn if string wrapper property has collation mismatching model's case-sensitivity (unless collation is explicit).\n- Feature: These now accept \"options\" parameter, which allows specifying collations for case-sensitive vs. ignore-case string wrappers.\n- Feature: ConfigureDomainModelConventions() now has convenience extensions CustomizeIdentityConventions()/CustomizeWrapperValueObjectConventions(), for easy custom conventions, e.g. based on core underlying type.\n\nPerformance:\n- Enhancement: Reduced assembly size: generic JSON serializers instead of generated ones.\n- Enhancement: Reduced assembly size: moved type-inferred Equals() and Compare() helpers out of generated code.\n- Enhancement: Source gen performance.\n\nMisc:\n- BREAKING: ValueObject comparison operators disallow null.\n- Semi-breaking: Entity<TId> now has ID-based ==/!=.\n- Semi-breaking: IFormattable & co for string wrappers have stopped treating null strings as \"\", to better reveal mistakes.\n- Semi-breaking: IIdentity implements IWrapperValueObject.\n- Semi-breaking: Wrappers/Identities generate no parameterized ctor if ANY ctor has params.\n- Feature: Analyzer and extensions for defined enums.\n- Feature: Non-generic Wrapper/Identity interfaces.\n- Feature: DummyBuilder RECORDS cloned on each step, for reuse.\n- Feature: Analyzer warns when '==' or similar implicitly casts some IValueObject to something else, to Avoid incorrect comparison.\n- Feature: Analyzer warns when '>' or similar operator risks unintended null handling.\n- Feature: Analyzer warns if field initializers might be skipped.\n- Fixed: Source-generated default ctor should not exist in case of primary ctor or lacking base default ctor.\n- Fixed: Source-generated records would ignore hand-written ToString()/Equals()/GetHashCode().\n- Fixed: Source-generated Wrappers/Identities would ignore hand-written explicit interface implementations.\n- Fixed: DummyBuilder gen would struggle with nested types.\n- Fixed: \"No source gen on nested type\" warning would not show.\n- Fixed: Custom attribute inheritance.\n- Enhancement: CompilerGeneratedAttribute throughout.\n- Enhancement: DebuggerDisplay for Wrappers/Identities.",
  "id": "Architect.DomainModeling",
